{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786915363155},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to calculate how many farmers markets the U.S. has per 100,000 residents. I need to:\n\n1. Get the total number of farmers markets from the first dataset\n2. Get the U.S. population from the census file\n3. Calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents to 4 decimal places\n4. Use tools to do the math and verify the result\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst instructions, I should:\n1. First check if there's a semantic model that might have this data\n2. List existing aliases in the catalog\n3. Ingest the two datasets as catalog aliases if they're not already there\n4. Compose a metric to calculate farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n5. Verify the result using xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by checking the catalog.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you calculate the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking the catalog, then ingest the data sources and compute this metric."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GHVR2oRxnaxWpyP67iXnNQ","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01Vt7ofhJzGFACaDwtAnNF5F","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":341,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8161,"totalTokens":8512,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0017050000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0.01020125,"total":0.01191625},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":189},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915363169,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78VLaVd5iWs6MVhQE1i","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01GHVR2oRxnaxWpyP67iXnNQ","toolName":"xorq_semantic_models","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No semantic models in this catalog — fall back to the ordinary ingest/compose flow."}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915366944},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01Vt7ofhJzGFACaDwtAnNF5F","toolName":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No aliases.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915366945},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog is empty. I need to ingest both datasets. Let me create build scripts under `.xorq/scripts/` to ingest these datasets.\n\n1. First, I'll ingest the farmers markets data from https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\n2. Then, I'll ingest the census population data from https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\n3. Then I'll compose a metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents\n4. Finally, I'll verify the result\n\nLet me start by creating the build scripts.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The catalog is empty, so I need to ingest both datasets. Let me create build scripts for each source."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_012SYdJr2uY2TN5VqEwnobMp","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"mkdir -p .xorq/scripts"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"output":268,"cacheRead":8161,"cacheWrite":438,"totalTokens":8881,"cost":{"input":0.000014,"output":0.00134,"cacheRead":0.0008161,"cacheWrite":0.0005475,"total":0.0027175999999999997},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":181},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915366945,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78VdDcm4KfqLPUig3Zg","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_012SYdJr2uY2TN5VqEwnobMp","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915369578},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll create the build script for the farmers markets dataset.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01BzVAUwJWaPtiPjr4ckbm9Z","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py","content":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    xo.duckdb_conn(),\n    storage_options=FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"xorq-analyst/1.0\"})\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":12,"output":201,"cacheRead":8599,"cacheWrite":291,"totalTokens":9103,"cost":{"input":0.000012,"output":0.001005,"cacheRead":0.0008599,"cacheWrite":0.00036375,"total":0.0022406500000000003},"cacheWrite1h":0,"reasoning":18},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786915369579,"responseId":"msg_011Ce78VoHbU14mu6PuQXKMy","rawStopReason":"tool_use"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_01BzVAUwJWaPtiPjr4ckbm9Z","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 251 bytes to .xorq/scripts/farmers_markets.py"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915371646},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me create a build script for the census population data.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01TBCEYwUTDEQ4yJhgAt6KnV","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/us_population.py","content":"import xorq as xo\nfrom frozendict import FrozenDict\n\nexpr = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST202